; A lazy parameter is put in where its routine is called (2026-10-18), and so
; far only a binary operator's is -- `operator and(left: bool, right: lazy
; bool)` in scaly/logic.scaly. A function's would be evaluated before the call
; without a word, so it is refused (Planner.plan_function#).
; xfail: a lazy parameter is so far taken only by a binary operator
function or_else(value: int, fallback: lazy int) returns int
    if value <> 0: value else fallback

print "`or_else(0, 5)`"
